# Example environment configuration. Copy to `.env.local` for local development.
# `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit real secrets.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# League password gate (per-league privacy bridge — see LEAGUE-PRIVACY-PASSWORD)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required whenever any league has a password set. The signing logic uses this
# value (HMAC-SHA256) to mint and verify the `league_auth_<slug>` session
# cookie. Generate a long random value:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Do NOT use a short or human-memorable value. There is no in-code default —
# the gate logic throws on missing/empty to fail loud.
LEAGUE_AUTH_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cron authentication (scheduled jobs in vercel.json)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token the scheduled cron routes require: /api/cron/season-transition,
# /api/cron/season-rollover, /api/cron/game-stats. The routes fail closed — a
# missing/unset value makes every scheduled run return 401, silently disabling
# automated season transition, rollover, and weekly game-stats ingestion.
# Generate a long random value:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database access — deliberately NOT in this file or in .env.local
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no DATABASE_URL here on purpose. Next.js auto-loads `.env.local`, so a
# connection string there would point `npm run dev` at PRODUCTION Neon. Dev is
# meant to run on the file-fallback store (`DATABASE_URL= npm run dev`).
#
# Operator/agent read-only production access lives in `.env.operator.local`
# (gitignored, never committed) as:
#
#   DATABASE_URL_RO=   # audit_ro role + RO endpoint, direct host (NOT -pooler)
#
# It is an observability rail, not part of the read path: `src/` contains no
# reference to it and must not gain one. Two independent guarantees — the
# `audit_ro` role holds only CONNECT/USAGE/SELECT, and the endpoint is read-only.
# See `docs/deployment-runbook.md` (read-replica section) for the full contract
# and the privilege probe to re-run rather than assume.
